  - q: "How secure is this password generator?"
    a: "This generator uses the Web Crypto API built into your browser to produce cryptographically secure random values. This is the same standard used by security professionals. The passwords are generated entirely on your device and never sent to any server."
  - q: "How long should a password be?"
    a: "Security researchers generally recommend at least 12 to 16 characters for most accounts, and 20 or more for financial or email accounts. Longer passwords are exponentially harder to crack than shorter ones. A 16-character random password is virtually impossible to brute-force with current computing power."
  - q: "Should I use special characters in passwords?"
    a: "Including symbols like punctuation marks and symbols significantly increases the number of possible character combinations, making passwords harder to guess. Not all websites accept every symbol, which is why this generator lets you toggle specific character types on and off."
  - q: "Where should I store the generated passwords?"
    a: "A reputable password manager is the safest option. Applications like Bitwarden, 1Password, and KeePass encrypt your passwords locally or in the cloud with strong encryption. Writing passwords on paper and keeping them secure is also safer than reusing the same password across sites."
